{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"<id-79>","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"IntelliJ Platform Gradle Plugin 2.19\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"blog.jetbrains.com\",\"url\":\"https://blog.jetbrains.com/platform/tag/gradle/\"},{\"title\":\"blog.jetbrains.com\",\"url\":\"https://blog.jetbrains.com/tag/gradle\"},{\"title\":\"gradle intellij plugin\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Tryweirder/gradle-intellij-plugin\"},{\"title\":\"IntelliJ Platform Plugin SDK Help\",\"url\":\"https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/tools-intellij-platform-gradle-plugin-extension.html\"},{\"title\":\"plugins.gradle.org\",\"url\":\"https://plugins.gradle.org/u/jetbrains\"},{\"title\":\"intellij platform gradle plugin\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-platform-gradle-plugin\"},{\"title\":\"plugins.gradle.org\",\"url\":\"https://plugins.gradle.org/search?page=23\"},{\"title\":\"plugins.gradle.org\",\"url\":\"https://plugins.gradle.org/search?page=301\"},{\"title\":\"IntelliJ Platform Gradle Plugin (2.x)\",\"url\":\"https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/tools-intellij-platform-gradle-plugin.html\"}]\n\nI couldn't find any results for a version 2.19 of the IntelliJ Platform Gradle Plugin. The closest data point is a Gradle Plugin Portal listing that shows 2.13.1 (14 March 2026) as the latest version, so 2.19 may not exist yet or may not be indexed.\n\nWhat the results do confirm about the 2.x line:\n\n- **Purpose:** It is a plugin for the Gradle build system to help configure environments for building, testing, verifying, and publishing plugins for IntelliJ-based IDEs. It is a successor of Gradle IntelliJ Plugin (1.x).\n- **Requirements:** The official docs list IntelliJ Platform: 2022.3 and Gradle: 8.2 as minimums, plus Java Runtime 17.\n- **Migration:** For users coming from 1.x, the docs say to change the plugin ID to org.jetbrains.intellij.platform.\n\nFor release notes or the exact latest version, check the official documentation at plugins.jetbrains.com or the Gradle Plugin Portal directly. I'd suggest a follow-up search for the plugin's GitHub releases page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<session_id-2>","uuid":"<uuid-95>","timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:15:41.376Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"IntelliJ Platform Gradle Plugin 2.19","results":[{"tool_use_id":"<tool_use_id-96>","content":[{"title":"blog.jetbrains.com","url":"https://blog.jetbrains.com/platform/tag/gradle/"},{"title":"blog.jetbrains.com","url":"https://blog.jetbrains.com/tag/gradle"},{"title":"gradle intellij plugin","url":"https://github.com/Tryweirder/gradle-intellij-plugin"},{"title":"IntelliJ Platform Plugin SDK Help","url":"https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/tools-intellij-platform-gradle-plugin-extension.html"},{"title":"plugins.gradle.org","url":"https://plugins.gradle.org/u/jetbrains"},{"title":"intellij platform gradle plugin","url":"https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-platform-gradle-plugin"},{"title":"plugins.gradle.org","url":"https://plugins.gradle.org/search?page=23"},{"title":"plugins.gradle.org","url":"https://plugins.gradle.org/search?page=301"},{"title":"IntelliJ Platform Gradle Plugin (2.x)","url":"https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/tools-intellij-platform-gradle-plugin.html"}]},"I couldn't find any results for a version 2.19 of the IntelliJ Platform Gradle Plugin. The closest data point is a Gradle Plugin Portal listing that shows 2.13.1 (14 March 2026) as the latest version, so 2.19 may not exist yet or may not be indexed.\n\nWhat the results do confirm about the 2.x line:\n\n- **Purpose:** It is a plugin for the Gradle build system to help configure environments for building, testing, verifying, and publishing plugins for IntelliJ-based IDEs. It is a successor of Gradle IntelliJ Plugin (1.x).\n- **Requirements:** The official docs list IntelliJ Platform: 2022.3 and Gradle: 8.2 as minimums, plus Java Runtime 17.\n- **Migration:** For users coming from 1.x, the docs say to change the plugin ID to org.jetbrains.intellij.platform.\n\nFor release notes or the exact latest version, check the official documentation at plugins.jetbrains.com or the Gradle Plugin Portal directly. I'd suggest a follow-up search for the plugin's GitHub releases page."],"durationSeconds":5.446652321000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"<id-79>","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_temporary"}}]}
